  "id": "wf4-verify-channel-blank-at-gate",
  "description": "If the Approval Gate emits a blank channel (empty string or whitespace), the branch halts with CHANNEL_UNRESOLVED before any send.",
  "why_it_exists": "D-CHANNEL-01 (2026-08-25). A blank channel is treated identically to NONE: the gate has no resolved channel to act on, so the branch must not continue. The old guard only checked for the literal string 'NONE' — a blank would have evaluated as U('') = '' which is neither equal to the row's channel nor equal to 'NONE', making the second term true and triggering CHANNEL_MISMATCH instead of CHANNEL_UNRESOLVED. The new guard treats blank (falsy after toUpperCase/trim) as unresolved.",
  "input": {
    "case_id": "C5E",
    "config": {
      "matter_id": "MAT-QA-CLEAN",
      "route_group": "APPROVAL",
      "approval_id": "APR-QACLEAN"
    },
